168 unreferenced Nagram resource files deleted after a full-tree
reference audit (R.<type>.<name> and @<type>/<name> for all 64 nagram
resources, code + XML + untracked files): launcher icon PNGs/XMLs and
layer drawables for the removed variants, nagram_notification PNGs +
vector, nagramx_outline*, ic_nagram_animated, nagram_* layer drawables
and the 3 values color files. Their only references were transitive
among themselves (adaptive-icon XMLs pointing at their own layers).

Kept deliberately:
- 4x nagramx_notification.png (hdpi/mdpi/xhdpi/xxhdpi): still used by
  SessionCell.java:364 as a session icon. Not deleted.
- R.string.Nagram ('Nagram', strings_na.xml): now unreferenced by code
  but left in place; removing strings from locale bundles is out of
  scope and harmless.

Re-pointed instead of deleted:
- NotificationsController.getNotificationIconResId case 2 now returns
  R.drawable.aligram_notification (was nagram_notification); settings
  label for option 2 is now 'AliGram' (R.string.NagramX already
  displays 'AliGram'). Options 1 and 2 are the same icon — both entries
  kept so stored preference values 0-3 keep their meaning.
- res/xml/auth.xml + contacts.xml icons now @mipmap/ic_launcher_aligram
  (_round) instead of the Nagram blue icons (AliGram icon exists in
  all densities); this is what made the blue PNGs deletable.
- NekoAboutActivity source-code row now opens
  https://github.com/tedfoagen-stack/AliGram (was risin42/NagramX).
  The @NagramX / @nagram_channel / @NagramTips rows and the NagramX
  Crowdin translation row were REMOVED, not re-pointed: no AliGram
  Telegram channel exists and none is invented; the About screen keeps
  the AliGram about row, the (re-pointed) source-code row and the
  datacenter row.
